.\" findjar(1) — search files and the contents of jar / zip / tar archives
.TH FINDJAR 1 "May 2026" "findjar" "User Commands"
.\" Disable groff's double-space after sentence-ending punctuation
.\" (".  It" rendered as ". It"). N=normal word space, M=extra after .?!
.ss 12 0
.SH NAME
findjar \- search files and the contents of jar, zip, and tar archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B findjar
.RI [ search-root ".\|.\|.] [" options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B findjar
searches files on disk and inside jar, zip, and tar (.tar / .tar.gz / .tgz) archives, with regex matching for file names, paths, and content.\&
It is intended for JVM developers tracking down classes, source files, or strings across a maven repo, classpath, or set of jars, but the archive-aware grep core is just as useful for tarballs, distro packages, and Python wheels' source dists.\&
With
.B \-\-nested
it also descends into jars-inside-jars (uberjars, Spring Boot fatjars, Pants/Bazel uberjars, etc.).\&

With no
.IR search-root ,
findjar searches the current directory.\&
Multiple
.IR search-root s
are scanned in order; result paths are prefixed with the root they came from so they are unambiguous between roots.\&

For paths inside archives, path patterns
.RB ( \-p ", " \-a )
match against
.IR <path-to-archive>@<path-within-archive> .\&
With
.BR \-\-nested ,
nested archives are joined with additional
.B @
separators:
.IR outer.jar@inner.jar@entry .

.SH OPTIONS

.SS Filtering
.TP
.BI \-n " regex" ", " \-\-name " regex"
Match against file name.
.TP
.BI \-p " regex" ", " \-\-path " regex"
Match against path relative to the search-root.
.TP
.BI \-a " regex" ", " \-\-apath " regex"
Match against absolute path.
.TP
.BI \-G " glob" ", " \-\-glob " glob"
Match against file name as a shell glob (e.g.
.IR \(dq*.clj\(dq )
instead of regex.\&
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-n .
.TP
.BI \-g " regex" ", " \-\-grep " regex"
Match against file content lines.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-word\-regexp
With
.BR \-g ,
match only at word boundaries: the pattern is wrapped in
.IR \eb...\eb .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-invert\-match
With
.BR \-g ,
emit lines that do NOT match the pattern.
.TP
.BI \-f " flags" ", " \-\-flags " flags"
Apply the given Pattern flag chars (i, m, s, u, x, d) to every regex.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-case
Shortcut for adding
.I i
to
.BR \-\-flags ;
the universal grep convention.\& Composes with
.BR \-f :
.B \-i \-f m
is equivalent to
.BR "\-f im" .
.TP
.BI \-t " types" ", " \-\-types " types"
Restrict file types: n (normal files), j (entries in jars), z (entries in zips), t (entries in .tar / .tar.gz / .tgz archives), g (contents of .gz files, e.g. rotated log files; entry path is foo.log.gz@foo.log).\& Default: nj.

.SS Action
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cat
Print the entire contents of matching files (with line numbers).
.TP
.B \-\-manifest
For each matched .jar/.zip entry whose path looks like
.I META-INF/MANIFEST.MF
or
.IR pom.properties ,
print its contents.\& Convenient one-step replacement for
.IR "findjar app.jar -t j -p MANIFEST -c" .
.TP
.B \-\-manifest\-summary
Like
.B \-\-manifest
but parses each MANIFEST.MF via java.util.jar.Manifest and keeps only
a curated allow-list of attributes most users care about (Main-Class,
Implementation-*, Bundle-*, Class-Path, Created-By, Built-By, etc.).\&
pom.properties entries are skipped (they are already a 3-line summary).\&
Useful for auditing what a fat jar bundles without paging through build
metadata.
.TP
.BI \-\-explode " dir"
Extract every matched entry to
.IR dir ,
preserving the archive layout: a path like
.I app.jar@BOOT-INF/lib/spring.jar@META-INF/MANIFEST.MF
is written to
.IR dir/app.jar/BOOT-INF/lib/spring.jar/META-INF/MANIFEST.MF .\&
Composes with
.BR \-n " / " \-p " / " \-\-nested " / " \-g
to narrow what gets extracted.\& Existing files are overwritten without
prompting; per-file extraction failures surface as warnings on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-class-info
For each matched .class entry, parse via ASM and print the class
name, access modifiers, super, implemented interfaces, and method
signatures.\& Combines naturally with
.B \-\-output json
to emit structured records.
.TP
.B \-\-count
With
.BR \-g ,
print only the count of matching lines per file.
.TP
.B \-\-max-count
Stop after
.I n
matching lines per file.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-files-only
With
.BR \-g ,
print one path per matching file instead of every matching line.
.TP
.BI \-s " algo" ", " \-\-hash " algo"
Print file hash.\& Output is
.IR \(dq<hex> <algo> <path>\(dq .\&
Algorithms: md5, sha1, sha256, sha512, crc32. Repeat
.B \-s
to print several.
.TP
.BI \-\-find\-by\-hash " algo:hex"
Find every file whose hash equals
.IR hex ;
e.g.
.IR sha1:da39a3ee...\& .\&
Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all output.\& Exit status 0 if any match was found, 1 otherwise.

.SS Output
.TP
.BI \-x " n" ", " \-\-context " n"
With
.BR \-g ,
show
.I n
lines of symmetric context around each match.
.TP
.BI \-A " n" ", " \-\-after " n"
With
.BR \-g ,
show
.I n
lines after each match.
.TP
.BI \-B " n" ", " \-\-before " n"
With
.BR \-g ,
show
.I n
lines before each match.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " fmt"
Output format:
.B text
(default),
.B json
(or its alias
.BR ndjson )
emitting one JSON object per line (JSON Lines / jsonl), or
.B json-array
emitting a single top-level JSON array (jq-friendly without
.BR "-s" ;
the array is empty when nothing matched).
.TP
.BI \-o " path" ", " \-\-out\-file " path"
With
.BR \-c ,
append output to
.I path
instead of stdout.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-monochrome
Disable ANSI coloring of matches.\& The
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable also disables coloring.
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
In path-listing modes (default action and
.BR \-l ),
terminate each emitted path with a NUL byte instead of a newline.\&
Pipes safely through
.B xargs \-0
even when paths contain spaces, quotes, or embedded newlines.

.SS Scanning
.TP
.B \-\-all
Traverse every directory.\& By default findjar skips
.IR .git ,
.IR .svn ,
.IR .hg ,
.IR .bzr ,
.IR node_modules ,
.IR target ,
.IR build ,
.IR .gradle ,
.IR .cpcache ,
.IR .idea ,
.IR .vscode ,
plus any paths matched by
.I .gitignore
at each search-root.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-follow
Follow symbolic links during traversal (default: don't follow).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-depth " n"
Do not descend more than
.I n
directory levels below each search-root.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " name"
Skip directories with this name.\& Repeatable; adds to the default exclude list.
.TP
.BI \-\-include\-glob " pattern"
Restrict the scan to candidate paths matching
.IR pattern ,
compared against the path relative to each search-root.\& Repeatable
(ANY-match).\& Globstar
.B **
matches any number of directory segments;
.B *
matches within one segment;
.B ?
matches a single character.\& Patterns apply at the filesystem level —
they decide whether an archive is opened, not which entries inside it
are scanned.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-glob " pattern"
Skip candidate paths matching
.IR pattern .\&
Same matching rules as
.BR \-\-include\-glob .\&
Any matching pattern excludes the path.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gitignore
Do not honor
.I .gitignore
files in search-roots.
.TP
.B \-\-text
With
.BR \-g ,
do not skip files that look binary (NUL bytes in the first 8 KB).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-parallel
Scan files serially.\& Default is parallel using ~ cores+2 workers.
.TP
.BI \-\-parallel\-jobs " n"
Cap the number of concurrent scan workers.\& Useful on HDD or networked filesystems.
.TP
.B \-\-nested
Recurse into jars/zips that appear as entries inside other jars/zips.\& Path takes the form
.IR outer.jar@inner.jar@entry .

.SS Misc
.TP
.B \-\-stats
After the scan, print a single summary line to stderr — number of
candidate paths examined, hits emitted, and wall-clock elapsed.\&
Useful when tuning
.B \-\-parallel\-jobs
or when a slow scan needs reassurance that work is happening.
.TP
.BI \-\-why\-skipped " path"
Diagnostic mode: instead of scanning, explain why
.I path
would NOT be picked up by the current flag set (default excludes,
.IR .gitignore ,
.BR \-\-types ,
.BR \-\-max\-depth ,
non-followed symlink in an ancestor, etc.).\& Prints one line per
search-root, then exits.\& Reasonable cure for "why isn't my file
matching?".
.TP
.B \-\-examples
Print usage examples and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-completions " shell"
Print a shell completion script
.RB ( zsh ", " bash ", or " fish )
to stdout.\& Embedded in the binary so a single-file install has
everything it needs:
.RS
.PP
.B findjar --completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_findjar
.PP
.B findjar --completions bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/findjar
.PP
.B findjar --completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/findjar.fish
.RE
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-profile
Enable tufte profiling.\& Developer flag; emits per-pass timing summaries to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Grep-compatible.
.TP
.B 0
At least one match was emitted.
.TP
.B 1
No match was found.
.TP
.B 2
Bad CLI args or other pre-scan error (e.g.
.IR "search root not found" ).
.PP
Note: per-file errors during a scan (unreadable jar, truncated archive)
are surfaced as warnings on stderr and do not change the exit status —
the status is decided solely by whether any match was emitted.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to a non-empty value, ANSI coloring is disabled (https://no-color.org).
.TP
.B FORCE_COLOR
If set to a non-empty value other than
.IR 0 ,
ANSI escape codes are emitted even when stdout is not a TTY (jansi
otherwise strips them on pipes / redirects).\& Useful for piping
findjar through pagers
.RB ( "less -R" )
or capturing colored output for terminal-rendering tools (asciinema,
svg-term-cli, freeze).
.B \-m
and
.B NO_COLOR
still win.
.TP
.B FINDJAR_DEBUG
If set, warning output includes the offending stack trace (otherwise
warnings emit only the message).

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Default to current directory:
.PP
.RS
findjar -g TODO
.RE
.PP
Glob match across a maven cache:
.PP
.RS
findjar ~/.m2 -G '*.clj'
.RE
.PP
Multi-algo hash for a file inside a jar:
.PP
.RS
findjar ~/.m2 -n string.clj -t j -s sha1 -s md5
.RE
.PP
Find every copy of a file by hash:
.PP
.RS
findjar ~/.m2 --find-by-hash sha1:da39a3ee5e6b4b0d3255bfef95601890afd80709
.RE
.PP
Recurse into uberjars:
.PP
.RS
findjar app.jar --nested -n MANIFEST.MF
.RE
.PP
Dump every fatjar's manifest (no need to know the META-INF path):
.PP
.RS
findjar app.jar --nested --manifest
.RE
.PP
Class-file structure (name, super, interfaces, methods):
.PP
.RS
findjar ~/.m2 -t j -n DataSourceConfig.class --class-info
.RE
.PP
JSON output for editor / jq pipelines:
.PP
.RS
findjar . -g TODO --output json | jq -s 'group_by(.path)'
.RE
.PP
List every class that implements a given interface (combine
.B \-\-class-info
with
.B \-\-output json
and
.IR jq ):
.PP
.RS
findjar ~/.m2 -t j --class-info --output json |
.br
\\ \\ \\ \\ jq 'select(.interfaces|index("java/io/Serializable"))|.name'
.RE
.PP
Search inside tar / tar.gz / tgz archives (system tarballs, distro
packages, Python wheels' source dist):
.PP
.RS
findjar ~/Downloads -t t -n setup.py
.RE

